1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:01,482
Eight lessons.

2
00:00:01,482 --> 00:00:02,254
Principles,

3
00:00:02,254 --> 00:00:02,956
pipelines,

4
00:00:02,956 --> 00:00:03,307
code,

5
00:00:03,307 --> 00:00:04,008
artifacts,

6
00:00:04,008 --> 00:00:04,640
security,

7
00:00:04,640 --> 00:00:05,201
metrics,

8
00:00:05,201 --> 00:00:06,043
bottlenecks,

9
00:00:06,043 --> 00:00:06,815
and a plan.

10
00:00:07,365 --> 00:00:09,596
But knowing is not the same as doing.

11
00:00:09,596 --> 00:00:11,104
So today is not a lesson.

12
00:00:11,104 --> 00:00:11,888
It is a test,

13
00:00:11,888 --> 00:00:13,999
and you will pass it with evidence.

14
00:00:14,549 --> 00:00:18,002
You will get a messy delivery review for CloudCart.

15
00:00:18,002 --> 00:00:18,865
Real numbers,

16
00:00:18,865 --> 00:00:19,994
one bad data row,

17
00:00:19,994 --> 00:00:21,056
and a job to do.

18
00:00:21,606 --> 00:00:22,267
By the end,

19
00:00:22,267 --> 00:00:23,830
you will have measured it,

20
00:00:23,830 --> 00:00:24,371
fixed it,

21
00:00:24,371 --> 00:00:25,032
planned it,

22
00:00:25,032 --> 00:00:25,934
and cleaned up.

23
00:00:25,934 --> 00:00:29,179
This is the mastery scenario for DevOps fundamentals.

24
00:00:30,729 --> 00:00:32,158
Here is what to expect.

25
00:00:32,708 --> 00:00:34,564
One: the scenario, and the rules.

26
00:00:35,114 --> 00:00:36,949
Two: the six jobs, in order.

27
00:00:37,499 --> 00:00:42,470
Three: a full live walk-through. You will see every step, including a mistake in the data.

28
00:00:43,020 --> 00:00:46,732
Four: the evidence you keep, where to find the files, and a self-check.

29
00:00:47,282 --> 00:00:50,738
And at the end, a look back at the whole domain, and what comes next.

30
00:00:52,788 --> 00:00:53,645
The scenario.

31
00:00:53,645 --> 00:00:55,557
CloudCart is an online shop.

32
00:00:55,557 --> 00:00:56,677
The team deploys,

33
00:00:56,677 --> 00:00:58,655
but nobody trusts the numbers.

34
00:00:59,205 --> 00:01:00,604
You are given two files.

35
00:01:00,604 --> 00:01:04,978
The first lists ten deploys over two weeks: when each change was committed,

36
00:01:04,978 --> 00:01:06,028
when it went live,

37
00:01:06,028 --> 00:01:07,311
and whether it failed.

38
00:01:07,861 --> 00:01:12,512
The second lists six pipeline stages, with hours of work and hours of waiting.

39
00:01:13,062 --> 00:01:16,066
Your job: find out how the team is really doing,

40
00:01:16,066 --> 00:01:17,255
find the slow step,

41
00:01:17,255 --> 00:01:18,694
and propose one change.

42
00:01:19,244 --> 00:01:19,985
One warning.

43
00:01:19,985 --> 00:01:21,776
One row in the data is wrong.

44
00:01:21,776 --> 00:01:26,284
A good engineer does not trust a number just because a script printed it.

45
00:01:27,834 --> 00:01:29,221
Six jobs, in order.

46
00:01:29,771 --> 00:01:33,077
One: measure the four key metrics, from lesson 150.

47
00:01:33,627 --> 00:01:37,403
Two: check the result. If a number looks too good, find out why.

48
00:01:37,953 --> 00:01:41,153
Three: fix the data, safely. Keep a copy first.

49
00:01:41,703 --> 00:01:46,183
Four: find the bottleneck, and the flow efficiency, from lesson 151.

50
00:01:46,733 --> 00:01:50,445
Five: write a plan with the six parts, from lesson 152.

51
00:01:50,995 --> 00:01:54,643
Six: write your report, run the check, and clean up after yourself.

52
00:01:56,193 --> 00:02:00,332
Go to the demo folder.

53
00:02:01,882 --> 00:02:03,780
Look around.

54
00:02:04,330 --> 00:02:09,493
Two data files, and four small tools. The same ones you met in the last three lessons.

55
00:02:10,043 --> 00:02:13,072
Job one: the four metrics.

56
00:02:14,222 --> 00:02:15,563
Five deploys a week.

57
00:02:15,563 --> 00:02:17,374
Lead time twenty-one hours.

58
00:02:17,374 --> 00:02:18,983
Twenty percent failures.

59
00:02:18,983 --> 00:02:21,262
And time to restore: half an hour.

60
00:02:21,812 --> 00:02:22,585
Half an hour?

61
00:02:22,585 --> 00:02:23,358
Two failures,

62
00:02:23,358 --> 00:02:24,844
restored in half an hour.

63
00:02:24,844 --> 00:02:26,033
That looks too good.

64
00:02:26,033 --> 00:02:27,103
Job two: check it.

65
00:02:27,653 --> 00:02:33,648
Job two: look at the failures.

66
00:02:34,198 --> 00:02:34,807
Two rows.

67
00:02:34,807 --> 00:02:35,484
The first,

68
00:02:35,484 --> 00:02:37,245
d three: deployed at nine,

69
00:02:37,245 --> 00:02:39,411
restored at eleven the next day.

70
00:02:39,411 --> 00:02:40,088
Two hours.

71
00:02:40,088 --> 00:02:40,427
Fine.

72
00:02:40,977 --> 00:02:41,728
The second,

73
00:02:41,728 --> 00:02:44,528
d seven: deployed on the eleventh at ten,

74
00:02:44,528 --> 00:02:46,782
restored on the eleventh at nine.

75
00:02:46,782 --> 00:02:48,967
Restored before it was deployed.

76
00:02:48,967 --> 00:02:50,265
That is impossible.

77
00:02:50,265 --> 00:02:51,494
The data is wrong.

78
00:02:52,044 --> 00:02:55,970
Job three: a safe copy.

79
00:02:57,320 --> 00:03:01,544
A scratch folder with the original. If we break something, we can go back.

80
00:03:02,094 --> 00:03:07,683
Fix the row.

81
00:03:08,233 --> 00:03:10,750
Measure again.

82
00:03:12,400 --> 00:03:14,284
Time to restore: three hours.

83
00:03:14,284 --> 00:03:15,128
Two failures,

84
00:03:15,128 --> 00:03:16,751
two hours and four hours.

85
00:03:16,751 --> 00:03:18,310
That is the real number.

86
00:03:18,860 --> 00:03:22,529
Job four: the bottleneck.

87
00:03:23,079 --> 00:03:24,798
The longest bar is review.

88
00:03:24,798 --> 00:03:25,657
Eleven hours,

89
00:03:25,657 --> 00:03:27,045
thirty-seven percent.

90
00:03:27,045 --> 00:03:27,905
Not approval,

91
00:03:27,905 --> 00:03:28,896
like last time.

92
00:03:28,896 --> 00:03:30,681
Every process is different,

93
00:03:30,681 --> 00:03:32,466
and that is why we measure.

94
00:03:33,016 --> 00:03:35,298
Flow efficiency: thirty-one percent.

95
00:03:35,848 --> 00:03:39,838
Job five: write the plan.

96
00:03:52,588 --> 00:03:57,388
Baseline, bottleneck, one change, target, measure, risk. The same six parts.

97
00:03:57,938 --> 00:04:02,140
Job six: the report.

98
00:04:10,190 --> 00:04:14,734
Seven lines. The metrics, the bottleneck, and what you found wrong in the data.

99
00:04:15,284 --> 00:04:18,804
Run the check.

100
00:04:19,354 --> 00:04:20,847
Eight of nine are fine.

101
00:04:20,847 --> 00:04:21,950
One fix: cleanup.

102
00:04:21,950 --> 00:04:24,157
The scratch folder is still there.

103
00:04:24,157 --> 00:04:25,520
That is the last job.

104
00:04:26,070 --> 00:04:31,275
Clean up.

105
00:04:31,825 --> 00:04:34,940
Check again.

106
00:04:35,490 --> 00:04:37,815
All nine. Mastery evidence complete.

107
00:04:39,365 --> 00:04:42,693
That is your mastery evidence. Let us name its three parts.

108
00:04:43,243 --> 00:04:44,791
One: documented results.

109
00:04:44,791 --> 00:04:46,727
Your report holds the numbers,

110
00:04:46,727 --> 00:04:48,856
and your plan holds the decision.

111
00:04:48,856 --> 00:04:50,211
Anyone can read them,

112
00:04:50,211 --> 00:04:51,179
and check them.

113
00:04:51,729 --> 00:04:52,921
Two: troubleshooting.

114
00:04:52,921 --> 00:04:54,170
You found a wrong row,

115
00:04:54,170 --> 00:04:56,044
because a result looked too good.

116
00:04:56,044 --> 00:04:57,747
You wrote down what was wrong.

117
00:04:57,747 --> 00:04:58,769
That is the habit.

118
00:04:59,319 --> 00:05:04,652
Three: cleanup. You removed what you created. A real engineer leaves no mess behind.

119
00:05:05,202 --> 00:05:06,878
And the check is independent.

120
00:05:06,878 --> 00:05:09,595
The script recomputes everything from the data.

121
00:05:09,595 --> 00:05:11,560
It does not take your word for it.

122
00:05:13,110 --> 00:05:15,478
A look back at the domain. Eight lessons.

123
00:05:16,028 --> 00:05:18,030
Principles: shared ownership,

124
00:05:18,030 --> 00:05:19,272
and fast feedback.

125
00:05:19,272 --> 00:05:20,170
Delivery: CI,

126
00:05:20,170 --> 00:05:21,551
continuous delivery,

127
00:05:21,551 --> 00:05:23,345
and continuous deployment.

128
00:05:23,895 --> 00:05:29,549
Automation: infrastructure as code, and one artifact promoted through every environment.

129
00:05:30,099 --> 00:05:34,088
Safety: shifting security left, error budgets, and platform thinking.

130
00:05:34,638 --> 00:05:39,161
And improvement: four metrics, find the bottleneck, make a plan, and run the loop.

131
00:05:39,711 --> 00:05:41,090
That is the foundation.

132
00:05:41,090 --> 00:05:42,709
Everything that comes next,

133
00:05:42,709 --> 00:05:43,309
the tools,

134
00:05:43,309 --> 00:05:45,108
will make sense because of it.

135
00:05:46,658 --> 00:05:50,477
Where to find the lab and demo files. Pause here, and write it down.

136
00:05:51,027 --> 00:05:56,701
One: the repository, github.com/it-waves/devops-ai.

137
00:05:57,251 --> 00:06:01,305
Two: the folder academy/lesson153-demo.

138
00:06:01,855 --> 00:06:05,887
Three: two data files, four tools, and a read me with the answers.

139
00:06:06,437 --> 00:06:10,767
Four: clone the repository, and copy the folder. You need a shell and awk.

140
00:06:11,317 --> 00:06:15,373
Five: the same repository holds every demo from this domain.

141
00:06:15,373 --> 00:06:18,144
Lessons 141 to 153.

142
00:06:20,194 --> 00:06:22,669
Check yourself. Six points. Tick each one.

143
00:06:23,219 --> 00:06:25,139
One: your metrics match the check.

144
00:06:25,689 --> 00:06:28,291
Two: you found the impossible row, and fixed it.

145
00:06:28,841 --> 00:06:31,124
Three: you kept a copy before editing.

146
00:06:31,674 --> 00:06:34,469
Four: the bottleneck and flow efficiency are right.

147
00:06:35,019 --> 00:06:36,768
Five: your plan says ready.

148
00:06:37,318 --> 00:06:40,817
Six: the scratch folder is gone, and all nine checks pass.

149
00:06:41,367 --> 00:06:44,417
All six, and you have mastered the DevOps fundamentals.

150
00:06:46,467 --> 00:06:48,238
Your turn, on your own machine.

151
00:06:48,788 --> 00:06:52,158
One: copy the demo folder. Do not look at the read me yet.

152
00:06:52,708 --> 00:06:55,716
Two: run the tools, and find the wrong row yourself.

153
00:06:56,266 --> 00:06:59,232
Three: write the plan and the report in your own words.

154
00:06:59,782 --> 00:07:02,192
Four: run the check, and fix what it flags.

155
00:07:02,742 --> 00:07:05,089
Five: clean up, and run it one more time.

156
00:07:05,639 --> 00:07:07,474
Pause the video, and begin now.

157
00:07:23,024 --> 00:07:23,899
Quick check.

158
00:07:24,449 --> 00:07:26,091
Why did we keep a copy first?

159
00:07:26,641 --> 00:07:28,412
What made us doubt the restore time?

160
00:07:28,962 --> 00:07:31,138
What are the three parts of mastery evidence?

161
00:07:31,688 --> 00:07:33,757
Why does the check recompute everything?

162
00:07:34,307 --> 00:07:39,449
Objective covered: MC16, mastery: a documented delivery review.

163
00:07:39,999 --> 00:07:42,068
Pause the video, and answer out loud.

164
00:07:52,618 --> 00:07:54,011
Next domain: Jenkins.

165
00:07:54,011 --> 00:07:55,801
We start doing it for real,

166
00:07:55,801 --> 00:07:56,929
with a real tool,

167
00:07:56,929 --> 00:07:58,719
and a real screen to click.

168
00:07:59,269 --> 00:08:02,597
If this helped, like, share and subscribe, so you do not miss it.
